# What data/CARD_MANIFEST.sha256 covers, and what it does not
#
# 178 of the 584 files in the 2026-09-30 card-corpus snapshot:
#   data/cards              144   the training corpus, every lo::/hi::/cell_*/pooled_* figure
#   data/prospective_cards   34   the prospective headline and every prosp_* key
#
# NOT COVERED, 406 files feeding 29 registry keys:
#   out/publisher_cards     260   the publisher census, 14 pub_* keys
#   out/lora_cards          136   the kurtosis/LoRA analysis, 11 lk_* keys
#   out/qwen35_cards         10   4 qwen35* keys
# Those three sets are pinned only inside the snapshot archive, which is
# outside git, so a clone cannot verify them. Recorded rather than implied
# covered; extending the manifest to them is cheap and not yet done.
#
# ORDERING. test_the_card_corpus_matches_its_committed_manifest verifies the
# hashes, but the re-harvest tests do NOT check them before running: they read
# whatever cards are present. So a corpus that fails the manifest and a
# re-harvest that passes can both be true in one run, and the manifest test is
# the one to believe. Making the re-harvest depend on the manifest check is
# the right fix and is not yet done.
